      "id": 1,
      "text": "Lovington was named after Andrew Love, the village’s first postmaster, when the town was founded in the mid‑1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lovington%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "James Kellar erected Lovington’s first building in 1838, a wooden structure that still marks the town’s origins.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lovingtonil.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lovington was officially incorporated as a village in 1873, solidifying its community status.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lovingtonil.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The local library houses a dedicated collection of Lovington’s history, preserving stories from early settlers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
